{"subjectId":"java","id":"modern-java","title":"Modern Java: 8 → 21 Feature Tour","group":"Design, Modern Java & Interview Prep","order":71,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">What changed from Java 8 to Java 21 — the features interviewers expect you to know and modern codebases actually use.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">LTS</div><p>Long-term-support releases: <strong>8, 11, 17, 21</strong> (and 25). Since Java 10 a feature release ships every six months; preview features need <code>--enable-preview</code>.</p></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-timeline\"></i>Feature timeline</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Version</th><th>Headline features</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>8</strong> (2014, LTS)</td><td>Lambdas, method references, Streams, <code>Optional</code>, <code>java.time</code>, default &amp; static interface methods, <code>CompletableFuture</code></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Module system (JPMS), <code>List.of</code> / <code>Set.of</code> / <code>Map.of</code>, JShell, private interface methods, <code>Stream.takeWhile</code>, compact strings</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><code>var</code> for local variables, <code>List.copyOf</code>, <code>Collectors.toUnmodifiableList</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>11</strong> (LTS)</td><td><code>String.isBlank/strip/repeat/lines</code>, <code>Files.readString/writeString</code>, standard <code>HttpClient</code>, single-file launch <code>java App.java</code>, <code>var</code> in lambda params</td></tr><tr><td>12–13</td><td><code>Collectors.teeing</code>, <code>String.indent/transform</code>; switch expressions &amp; text blocks in preview</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td><strong>Switch expressions</strong> (<code>-&gt;</code>, <code>yield</code>), helpful <code>NullPointerException</code> messages</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td><strong>Text blocks</strong> <code>\"\"\"</code>, <code>String.formatted</code>, ZGC production-ready</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td><strong>Records</strong>, <strong>pattern matching for <code>instanceof</code></strong>, <code>Stream.toList()</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>17</strong> (LTS)</td><td><strong>Sealed classes</strong>, strong encapsulation of JDK internals, <code>RandomGenerator</code></td></tr><tr><td>18–20</td><td>UTF-8 by default, simple web server <code>jwebserver</code>; previews of virtual threads, record patterns</td></tr><tr><td><strong>21</strong> (LTS)</td><td><strong>Virtual threads</strong>, <strong>pattern matching for <code>switch</code></strong>, <strong>record patterns</strong>, <strong>sequenced collections</strong> (<code>getFirst</code>, <code>reversed</code>), generational ZGC</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>Many features, one program</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class Main {\n    sealed interface Shape permits Circle, Rect {}             // 17: sealed\n    record Circle(double r) implements Shape {}                 // 16: records\n    record Rect(double w, double h) implements Shape {}\n\n    static String describe(Object o) {\n        return switch (o) {                                     // 21: pattern switch\n            case Circle(double r) when r &gt; 10 -&gt; \"big circle\";  // 21: record pattern + guard\n            case Circle c -&gt; \"circle r=\" + c.r();\n            case Rect(double w, double h) -&gt; \"rect \" + (w * h);\n            case String s -&gt; \"text of length \" + s.length();\n            case null -&gt; \"null!\";\n            default -&gt; \"something else\";\n        };\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        var shapes = List.of(new Circle(2), new Rect(3, 4), new Circle(20));   // 10: var, 9: List.of\n        shapes.forEach(s -&gt; System.out.println(describe(s)));                 // 8: lambdas\n        System.out.println(describe(\"hi\") + \", \" + describe(null));\n\n        Object o = shapes.get(1);\n        if (o instanceof Rect r &amp;&amp; r.w() &lt; r.h()) {                             // 16: instanceof pattern\n            System.out.println(\"tall \" + r);\n        }\n\n        String json = \"\"\"\n                {\"name\": \"%s\", \"ok\": %b}\"\"\".formatted(\"java\", true);          // 15: text block + formatted\n        System.out.println(json);\n\n        System.out.println(\"  hi  \".strip() + \"|\" + \"ab\".repeat(3) + \"|\" + \"   \".isBlank());   // 11\n\n        var names = new ArrayList&lt;&gt;(List.of(\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"));\n        System.out.println(names.getFirst() + names.getLast() + \" \" + names.reversed());    // 21: sequenced\n\n        List&lt;String&gt; kinds = shapes.stream().map(s -&gt; s.getClass().getSimpleName()).toList();   // 16: toList()\n        System.out.println(kinds);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>circle r=2.0\nrect 12.0\nbig circle\ntext of length 2, null!\ntall Rect[w=3.0, h=4.0]\n{\"name\": \"java\", \"ok\": true}\nhi|ababab|true\nac [c, b, a]\n[Circle, Rect, Circle]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bug\"></i>Helpful NullPointerExceptions (14+)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    record Address(String city) {}\n    record User(Address address) {}\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        User u = new User(null);\n        try {\n            System.out.println(u.address().city().length());\n        } catch (NullPointerException e) {\n            System.out.println(e.getMessage());\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>Cannot invoke \"Main$Address.city()\" because the return value of \"Main$User.address()\" is null</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brand-threads\"></i>Virtual threads (21)</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>import java.util.concurrent.Executors;\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        AtomicInteger done = new AtomicInteger();\n        try (var executor = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {\n            for (int i = 0; i &lt; 10_000; i++) {\n                executor.submit(() -&gt; {\n                    Thread.sleep(10);                 // blocking is cheap on a virtual thread\n                    return done.incrementAndGet();\n                });\n            }\n        }                                             // close() waits for all tasks\n        System.out.println(\"completed: \" + done.get());\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>completed: 10000</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Which Java version would you pick for a new project and why?</summary><div><p>The latest LTS (21, or 25 if the stack supports it): records, sealed types, pattern matching and virtual threads are all final, and it gets long-term security updates. Frameworks like Spring Boot 3 require at least 17.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What are the headline features of Java 8?</summary><div><p>Lambda expressions and functional interfaces, method references, the Streams API, <code>Optional</code>, the <code>java.time</code> API, default and static methods in interfaces, and <code>CompletableFuture</code>.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What is pattern matching in Java 21?</summary><div><p><code>switch</code> can test the <em>type</em> of the selector (<code>case String s -&gt;</code>), deconstruct records (<code>case Point(int x, int y) -&gt;</code>), add guards (<code>when x &gt; 0</code>) and handle <code>case null</code>. With sealed hierarchies, the compiler checks exhaustiveness so no <code>default</code> is needed.</p></div></details></section>"}